      "title": "Page 6",
      "pageStart": 6,
      "pageEnd": 6,
      "target": "../sections/page-006.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "1.1 [JSON-LD11] and is a key enabler of this specification, allowing for the same natural PROV\nproperty names to be used in different contexts while still maintaining their correct mappings to the\nappropriate RDF properties.\nThus, this specification proposes PROV-JSONLD, a PROV serialization compatible with [PROV-DM]\nthat addresses all of our 4 key requirements. It is, first and foremost, a JSON structure supporting\nlightweight Web applications. It is structured so that each PROV expression is encoded as a self-\ncontained JSON object and, therefore, is natural to JavaScript programmers. Exploi",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/w3c-2024-prov-jsonld/blocks/prose-page-007",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Page 7",
      "pageStart": 7,
      "pageEnd": 7,
      "target": "../sections/page-007.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "This section is non-normative.\nWe assume the reader to be familiar with PROV, JSON, and JSON-LD.\nTo illustrate the PROV-JSONLD serialization, we consider a subset of the example of [PROV-\nPRIMER], depicted below. It can be paraphrased as follows: agent Derek was responsible for\ncomposing an article based on an existing dataset.\ncompose\ndataSet1\nuse\nderek\nassoc\narticle1\ngen\nder\ntitle: Crime rises in cities@EN\ntype:\nprov:Person\nmbox:\n<mailto:derek@example.org>\ngivenName: Derek\nFigure 1: Provenance expressing that Derek was responsible for composing an article based on a data\nset.\nThe PROV-JSONLD",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/w3c-2024-prov-jsonld/blocks/prose-page-008",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Page 8",
      "pageStart": 8,
      "pageEnd": 8,
      "target": "../sections/page-008.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "PROV expressions can be enriched with various properties. Some properties are predefined by PROV-\nJSONLD such as activity and agent in a Association. Further PROV attributes are allowed, for\ninstance type with an array of further types, to better describe the resource. Others may be defined in a\ndifferent namespace such as foaf:givenName, for which we expect the prefix foaf to be declared in the\n@context property.\nThe property @type is mandatory and is associated with a single value, expected to be one of the\npredefined PROV expressions. From an efficiency viewpoint, this property is critical",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/w3c-2024-prov-jsonld/blocks/prose-page-009",
